WEBVTT

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:12.580
Someday... Yes, someday,

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.000
I'll be walking down

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.950
"Episode 12: 'Friends and Love,
Love and Cherry Blossoms'"

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.950
a spring path while looking up at the
cherry blossoms whether I want to or not.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.620
I'm a normal person.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.080
I don't have the ability to
touch something I can't see,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.660
and I can't involve myself in something
that's not happening right in front of me.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.160
What I'm scared of is while I'm not looking

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.290
Shimamura will change into something different.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:48.160
So I've made up my mind to spend
every spare moment looking at Shimamura.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.250
Um... Adachi.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:54.080
Yes?

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.120
--Pssh, pssh, pssh...

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.290
--Never mind.
--Pssh, pssh, pssh...

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.750
Heyo, Shima!

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.000
Hey, Adachicchi is with you, too.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.500
Chicchi!

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.950
Hey, Hino and Nagafuji. It's been a while.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.870
It sure has!

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.330
Did you change your shampoo, Nagafuji?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:16.870
Well, I spent the night
at Hino's place yesterday,

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:19.080
and took a bath there this morning.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.790
Huh...?

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:24.790
Look, you don't really
have to talk about that now.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.910
Come on, it's our turn.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.000
Okay.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.580
--Good luck out there.
--Pssh, pssh, pssh, pssh, pssh...

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.700
Staying at someone's house...

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.410
Then using their bath and then
heading right to school...

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:42.450
C-Can I come over, too?

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.580
Huh?

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.040
And spend the night.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.830
Uh, at Hino's place?

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:53.040
Y-Your place, Shimamura.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.910
Why?

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.040
Well, uh...

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:02.950
I mean, our bathtub's tiny.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.040
I don't really care about the bath.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.910
Wait, do I? No, I think it does matter...

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.580
Maybe it does matter...

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.580
Adachi?

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:27.450
That doesn't really matter...
But I want to spend the night!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.790
But why?

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:34.080
B-Because I want to be
closer to you, Shimamura...

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.200
Are we not close already? I had no idea.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.200
No, we are, we are!

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.540
I think... But I want to be closer.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.700
Do you get closer by spending the night, though?

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.580
Well, whatever.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.540
A-Adachi?

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.370
Under the pretense of discussing
me spending the night,

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:13.200
I got to hang out with Shimamura
after school... Wow.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.160
Spending the night is awesome.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.790
So...

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:20.700
Do you want to come over to
my place this Saturday or Sunday?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.830
T-Two days off...

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.750
And spending the night two nights...

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.410
You want to stay at my place that long?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.540
Just so you know, my place isn't an inn.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.540
What about work?

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.870
I'll go to work... um, from your place.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.870
Mm-hm.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:44.500
Though there's probably going to be
one more when we get to my place.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:50.450
I'm not sure why, but it feels like
I have two or three little sisters now.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.660
You mean me, too?

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.160
Her little sister... Shimamura Sakura.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.580
It's like an alliteration.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:07.830
We'd be even closer than friends then,

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.370
and that part's fine...

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:16.000
But then I think we'd get too close
and she'd notice me even less.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.330
"Change of underwear
Socks 4? 5?
Food: Bread & Instant ramen"

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.250
"Change of underwear
Socks 4? 5?
Food: Bread & Instant ramen"

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:20.250
Here's all the stuff I'll need to buy...

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:25.580
And then, I just need something to
make sure Shimamura doesn't get bored.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.620
Yeah, that's not going to work.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:39.000
If we can't think of anything to do,
I guess we can just watch TV together.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:44.580
Maybe, just maybe...

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:49.410
The same thing will happen and hopefully,
I won't run away again.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.750
I'm not going to run away!

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.290
G-Good morning...

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.290
You know...

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.950
Uh... You seem to have a lot of stuff.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:21.660
You do realize you're not moving, right?
It's a bit much.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.160
You think so?

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:28.540
Also, aren't you early? It's still 8 AM.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.120
S-Sorry. Were you sleeping?

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.200
Yup, you woke me up.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.120
Sorry.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.450
Eh, it's fine.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:41.620
You're always so punctual, Adachi. That's good.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:46.750
I was actually here at 7 AM,
but I figured that was a bit too early.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:50.250
I can't tell her I was just wandering
around on my bike for an hour.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:54.790
That's probably the only
weird part of this, so...

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.830
Anyway, welcome.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.370
Come in.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.450
Th-Thanks...

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.750
You remember my friend, don't you?

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:16.120
H-Hi...

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.450
She's being a good girl today.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:25.160
Is the room upstairs okay? Or well...
That's the only open room we have.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.620
Oh? Did you not want to go upstairs?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.620
Not exactly...

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.750
I guess I won't be staying
in the same room as you...

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.910
You want to stay in the same room as me?

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:47.620
I'm fine with it, but I don't think
my little sister will like that. Sorry.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:56.040
There was no way this was
all going to go as I planned.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:01.160
I'm not sure if Shimamura's okay
with me staying in her room...

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:05.700
I'm fine with it, but I don't think
my little sister will like that.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.750
I'm fine with it... I'm fine with it...

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.870
Or maybe she is!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.290
Y-Yes?

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.910
What do you want to do for breakfast?
Did you already eat?

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.910
Don't worry. I came prepared.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.200
"Long Long Sticks"

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.910
Hey, hey, hey...

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.370
What? My cooking's not good enough for you?

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:33.540
Oh, no. I'll have some. Thank you very much...

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.040
Dig in.

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:40.040
So, Adachi,

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.660
you probably actually go to school
unlike this daughter of mine.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.040
No, I, uh...

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.040
Adachi's in the same boat.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.620
Oh, really?

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:54.250
She looks like a nice, quiet girl,
unlike my delinquent over here.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:56.580
Oh, shut up.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:01.450
Shimamura's more of a good girl than I am.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:02.700
Good girl...?

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:09.410
I see. So you must be older, Adachi.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:13.160
That's not true.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:28.120
Thanks for the grub.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:31.750
Come in.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.290
Um, are you mad?

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.790
About what?

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:45.790
Oh, earlier? My mom's always like that,
so there's no point in getting mad.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.160
So that's just how their relationship is.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:51.750
More importantly, Adachi...

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.580
What should we do now?

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:59.200
I wonder how long it's been
since I was able to feel

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.750
that days off were actually special?

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:06.120
Yesterday, the first day I stayed over,

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.370
really did end with nothing happening.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:15.620
W-Well, I'll see you later.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.500
Have a good day!

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.250
Thanks.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:26.330
Nothing special with Shimamura
actually happened.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.330
We were just there together.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:32.330
--Just being with her might
just be ideal to me, but...
--Meat was really cheap
at the supermarket today.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:36.790
--Just being with her might
just be ideal to me, but...

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.200
But...

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:45.500
I-I'm going to do my best!

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:54.250
Yeah, you do that.

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.660
Shimamura laughed.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.540
Today might be a good day after all.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.870
But then again,

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:07.290
it's not like absolutely
nothing happened yesterday.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.160
Not exactly.

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:14.620
Hogetsu, hurry up, and take a bath.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:17.200
You go right to bed whenever you get full.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:20.830
Yeah, yeah, sure.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:23.500
Thank you for the meal...

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:29.830
Really? You brought that, too?

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:32.410
Shimamura's room is on the first floor,

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.620
--You're too polite, Adachi.
You could've just used ours.
--but she naturally came to my room.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:36.660
--You're too polite, Adachi.
You could've just used ours.
--That made me so happy.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:38.790
--B-But I wanted to cause you
the least amount of trouble.
--That made me so happy.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.160
--B-But I wanted to cause you
the least amount of trouble.
--I'm not exactly towards who,

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.330
but I felt superior towards them.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:49.040
So, at that moment...

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:52.500
I got a little bold.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:57.080
Can I... um, sit between your legs?

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.080
As long as you don't

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:02.790
run away this time.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.330
Here you go.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:09.160
O-Okay, sure.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.250
D-Don't mind if I do...

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:19.830
You're not going to scooch closer?

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.540
Sure. Then, excuse me.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.000
So soft... Eek.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:33.450
Th-There's no reason to panic.
Shimamura's a girl, but so am I... yeah.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:41.700
Sh-Shimamura...

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:49.870
I guess she does fall asleep
right after eating...

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:07.790
Huh? What's up? Why do you have
a change of clothes?

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.790
Oh, a bath.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:13.700
You want to take one first? That's rare.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.750
Let's take one together.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:21.120
Huh? Where'd that come from?
I thought you said you're embarrassed to.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:24.330
It's okay sometimes... Come on.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.870
Huh? Wait...

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.580
Uh...

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.580
I guess I'm going...

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:42.500
Shimamura...

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:43.910
Stop daydreaming.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:45.370
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:51.700
Ahem. Thanks for having me over...
or maybe I should say, "I'm home."

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.580
Oh, Adachi?

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.040
Y-Yes!

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.910
Well, well, welcome home.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:00.870
I-I've returned...

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:05.040
My daughter's out right now.
She said something about shopping.

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:06.910
Oh, I see.

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:09.290
She should be back soon, though.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:11.540
She can be pretty lazy.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:17.160
She's always been a sleepyhead
ever since she was little.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:20.830
She really does sleep a lot like a koala.

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:25.540
Oh, yeah. How's she doing at school?

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:29.040
Is she actually going to class?

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:30.450
Y-Yes...

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:35.160
Well, that's good. She tends to be lazy,

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.160
so it must be hard to get her to do anything.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.250
Huh? Not at all. Actually, it's the opposite.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.290
The opposite?

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:47.160
She always leads... Is that the right word?
She always leads me around.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.330
That's actually surprising.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:53.500
I'm home. Oh, welcome back, Adachi.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.910
I'm back.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.910
WB.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.160
I see you're both enjoying some <i>dango</i>.

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.700
You didn't say anything weird to her, did you?

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.410
I guess upstairs works.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.250
Now that I look at it,

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:16.160
I think "lead" really was the right term.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:22.040
I pretty much follow Shimamura
around like her little puppy dog.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.950
Oh, sit there.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.370
O-Okay.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:30.120
Now, lower your head and bend down a bit.

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:32.870
Huh? L-Like this?

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:35.330
Stay just like that for a sec.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.750
And then, we go like this...

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:50.200
And there we go.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:54.580
Yup. Now you have the same hairstyle as me.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.910
A moment, please.

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:01.870
Here.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:05.500
My hair color's starting to match yours,

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.950
so I figured we'd end up looking a lot alike.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:14.700
Let's see... Hm.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:20.250
Maybe we don't look that much alike.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.620
Oh, yeah. You can have that hairclip.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:25.540
Huh?

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:26.700
But that...

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.200
But that...

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:34.120
But that means we're matching!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:49.410
I-I... Sh-Shimamura, I...

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:54.950
I... wuv...

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:59.660
You look wuvly!

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.500
Wuvly, eh?

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:06.790
You look lovely, yes.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:11.200
We did this before, by the way.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.790
Mm...

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.620
You're so funny.

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.080
Let's stretch out those cheeks.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.500
L-Let's not.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:30.500
Shimamura.

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:35.580
So today...

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:42.000
Do you want to sleep together today?!

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.080
Uh, sure?

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:50.620
She didn't even hesitate. Then actually...

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:55.450
I should've suggested this yesterday, too!

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.950
But will it be okay?

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.040
What?

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.580
Your sister sleeping on her own.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.540
Oh, don't worry.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:12.290
Because she has a friend
sleeping over today, too.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.000
Little?

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:21.540
I shall teach you about the universe, Little.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.830
Th-The universe?

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.580
Yes.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:30.790
First, my kind tends to live
an average of 800 million years,

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:34.870
so I belong to species
that lives for a much longer time.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.450
And...

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.000
Okay, I'm turning off the lights.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.250
Okay.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:44.040
Night.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.620
What's wrong?

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:36.620
I-I was just wondering if you
were really asleep...

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:40.000
Well, yeah. I'm in my futon.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.370
Right...

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:45.830
I don't want to grow more
distant with Shimamura.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:50.500
Three, two, one. My courage
is trying to tell me to go.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:54.450
My courage is taking the initiative,
and kicking me in the ass.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:04.040
You fell like a bug.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:09.830
Want to sleep together?

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:14.830
The universe... The universe...

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:20.120
How do you like your Big Sis's shoulder pillow?

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.160
I...

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.290
I?

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:24.000
I feel like I'm going to cry.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:29.660
Your hair's still a bit wet.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:36.830
There's something about that warmth
you feel when it's wet that feels nice.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:39.700
Can I have my arm back now?

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:41.040
Not yet.

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:43.330
How much longer?

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:46.250
Until I fall asleep.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.330
What am I ever going to do with you?

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.870
Oh, yeah. We're changing desks tomorrow.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.290
Huh? We are?

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:57.370
Oh, you didn't know
because you skipped class.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.330
Adachi?

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:05.160
It'd be great if we could sit this close.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:10.000
Er, I'm sure there'd be a few
problems if we sat this close...

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:14.790
What will be, will be.

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:25.250
Let's eat lunch together tomorrow.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:30.080
Yeah, of course. So relax, and go to sleep.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:36.330
Adachi... Goodnight.

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:39.000
Goodnight.

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:53.000
We're heading out.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.290
Hold your horses.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:59.580
Take these with you.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:01.160
What are these?

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:04.000
Can't you tell?

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:07.080
Packed lunches are making a comeback!

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.660
Wait, why though?

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.790
Ugh, why are you such a pain?!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:20.450
By the way, I think this is the first time
we've gone to school together.

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:22.120
I think so.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:38.500
Please let me sit near Shimamura.
Please let me sit near Shimamura.

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:42.790
Please let me sit near Shimamura...

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:44.950
Please let me...

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:51.500
I wonder how much praying
actually helps in real life.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.950
Adachi, eyes up front.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:01.580
I guess finding that out is half the fun.

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:09.080
Yeah, this is sorta plain.

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:15.620
It's not like we got that much closer,
and we didn't move that much away.

00:22:17.660 --> 00:22:18.500
"Delinquent" "Adachi"

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:21.410
"Delinquent" "Adachi"

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:21.410
And before I knew it, it had already been
a month since we became second-years.

00:22:21.410 --> 00:22:24.910
And before I knew it, it had already been
a month since we became second-years.

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:29.660
I'll only have one more April in high school.

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:37.750
Then it'll be May, then June...
The time we have isn't infinite.

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:41.410
Yummy!

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:45.450
Someday... Yes, someday,

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:48.000
even if I can't imagine it clearly,

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:52.500
the future is inevitable. A world
where there'll be no spring breaks.

00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:56.910
Or perhaps, a future where
there's no one next to me.

00:22:56.910 --> 00:22:58.450
I'll be walking down

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:04.870
a spring path while looking up at the
cherry blossoms whether I want to or not.

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:10.040
Shimamura!

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:18.450
And until then,

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:23.160
I guess I'll settle for the cherry blossom
that's right in front of me.

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:25.830
I don't mind it at all.

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:32.160
It's the end of April. There aren't
any more cherry blossoms anywhere.

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:37.080
And that's why... I'll need Adachi
to be my cherry blossom.

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:48.910
Her profile will always...
